window.PYQ_OCR['nabard-a'].push({t:'nabard a 2021 computer',q:[{"n": 51, "q": "What is the full form of URL?", "o": ["Universal Resource Locator", "Uniform Resource Locator", "Union Research Locator", "Union Resource Locator (e) Uniform Research Locator Answer – (b) Explanation - This is a factual question wherein the options are very similar. A URL is nothing more than the address of a given unique resource on the Web."], "a": null}, {"n": 52, "q": "Which of the following options is available in the share ribbon of file explorer in windows 10?", "o": ["Sorting and arranging contents of the folder", "Adding additional panels to show a preview or details of the files", "Verifying/modifying properties of a document", "Print & Fax (e) Renaming a file or folder Answer – (d) Explanation - Under the share tab(ribbon) of File Explorer in Windows 10, we find the following options: 1. Burn to Disc 2. Print 3. Fax 4. Share 5. Zip"], "a": null}, {"n": 53, "q": "How many holes are there in a VGA connector?", "o": ["9", "11", "13", "15 (e) 17 Answer – (d) Explanation - The VGA connector is used for display devices and is used to connect a computer to a monitor, projector, or TV. The VGA connector has 15 holes, and each hole (pin) has its own function."], "a": null}, {"n": 54, "q": "_____ is found just above the file tab option in MS word. Its purpose is to provide a convenient access to most commonly used commands.", "o": ["Document area", "Quick access toolbar", "Ribbon", "Title bar (e) Ruler Answer – (b) Explanation - Quick Access Toolbar lies next to the Microsoft Office Button. It is a customizable toolbar that comes with a set of independent commands. It gives you quick access to commonly used commands such as Save, Undo, Redo, etc. When you click the drop-down arrow next to toolbar it offers more commands."], "a": null}, {"n": 55, "q": "In MS Excel, to reach to the last cell of the worksheet that contains data, which of the following shortcut key is used?", "o": ["Ctrl + T", "Ctrl + W", "Ctrl + ]", "Ctrl + End (e) Ctrl + E Answer – (d) Explanation - In Microsoft Excel, pressing Ctrl + End moves to the last cell containing text."], "a": null}, {"n": 56, "q": "_____ file operation is simply deleting the file except deleting the attributes.", "o": ["Close", "Seek", "Delete", "Append (e) Truncate Answer – (e) Explanation - Truncating is simply deleting the file except deleting attributes."], "a": null}, {"n": 57, "q": "The length of IPv4 address is", "o": ["64-bit", "32-bit", "128-bit", "256-bit (e) 16-bit Answer – (b) Explanation - IPv4 is composed of 32-bit address length and is the fourth version of the Internet Protocol (IP)."], "a": null}, {"n": 58, "q": "______ is a type of device that acts as the central point among computers and other devices that are a part of a network.", "o": ["Distributor", "Router", "USB", "Network card (e) Network cable Answer – (b) Explanation - A router is a device that connects two or more packet-switched networks or sub-networks. It serves two primary functions: managing traffic between these networks by forwarding data packets to their intended IP addresses, and allowing multiple devices to use the same Internet connection."], "a": null}, {"n": 59, "q": "Starting a computer or a computer embedded device is called –", "o": ["Signing", "Logging", "Spoofing", "Booting (e) Threading Answer – (d) Explanation - Booting is the process of starting a computer. It refers to loading an operating system (OS) into the computer’s main memory or RAM."], "a": null}, {"n": 60, "q": "Language used in second generation computers is called", "o": ["Basic", "Pascal", "Machine Language", "Algol (e) Assembly language Answer – (e) Explanation - Assembly language is a type of programming language that directly interacts with a computer's hardware. It enables software developers to write code using more understandable words and expressions, rather than the binary or hexadecimal data that the computer uses to store and process information."], "a": null}, {"n": 61, "q": "The ‘Header and Footer’ option in MS-Word is present under which tab?", "o": ["Mailing", "Insert", "Home", "File (e) Review Answer – (b) Explanation - Insert Tab is used to insert or add extra features in your document. It is commonly used to add tables, pictures, clip art, shapes, page number, etc."], "a": null}, {"n": 62, "q": "Which of the following registers holds the address of an instruction?", "o": ["Temporary register", "Accumulator", "Address register", "Data register (e) Program counter Answer – (e) Explanation - A program counter (PC) is a CPU register in the computer processor which has the address of the next instruction to be executed from memory."], "a": null}, {"n": 63, "q": "The difference between the arrival time and the time at which the process first gets the CPU is called _____ Time.", "o": ["Turn around", "Event", "Burst", "Response (e) Wait Answer – (d) Explanation - Response time is the time spent when the process is in the ready state and gets the CPU for the first time."], "a": null}, {"n": 64, "q": "Which MS excel function calculates the number of days between 2 dates?", "o": ["GAP", "DATES", "DAYS", "DAYS360 (e) SPAN Answer – (c) Explanation - The Excel DAYS function is a formula that calculates the number of days between two dates. The function appears as follows: \"=DAYS(end_date, start_date).\""], "a": null}, {"n": 65, "q": "Create, insert and write, preview results and finish are commands found in which tab of MS word 2013?", "o": ["Mailing tab", "Home tab", "Reference tab", "Review tab (e) Page layout tab Answer – (a) Explanation - Mailing Tab, placed between References and Review Tab, is divided into multiple sections with the name Create, Start Mail Merge, Write & Insert Fields, Preview Results and Finish."], "a": null}, {"n": 67, "q": "_____ method can make macros run automatically in MS-excel 2013, once you have done some setup for scheduling a macros.", "o": ["Application now", "Application offline", "Ontime", "Uptime (e) Time zone Answer – (c) Explanation - Application. OnTime method schedules a macro/procedure to be run at a specified time in the future (either at a specific time of day or after a specific amount of time has passed)."], "a": null}, {"n": 68, "q": "________type of Column chart in MS-Excel 2013 is like a stacked column. It uses a single bar for each category and subdivides that bar to show the proportion from each series.", "o": ["3-D column", "Clustered", "3-D clustered", "100% stacked (e) Histogram Answer – (d) Explanation - A 100% stacked column chart is an Excel chart type meant to show the relative percentage of multiple data series in stacked columns, where the total (cumulative) of stacked columns always equals 100%."], "a": null}, {"n": 69, "q": "____ contains the code, by executing which the CPU access the very first partition of hard disk when we turn on the computer.", "o": ["ROM", "DOS", "EHD", "DDS (e) BIOS Answer – (e) Explanation - A type of firmware called the Basic Input/Output System (BIOS) is needed to start up a computer and configure its hardware. It is the first piece of code a computer runs when it is switched on, and is kept in a chip on the motherboard."], "a": null}, {"n": 70, "q": "What is the storage capacity of a dual layered Blue ray disc?", "o": ["50 GB", "25 GB", "100 GB", "20 GB (e) 200 GB Answer – (a) Explanation - Blu-ray discs can be single-layer or dual-layer. A single-layer disc has 25 GB and a dual-layer disc has 50 GB storage capacity. Free Ebooks Current Affairs Download Now Explore Now FREE MOCK TESTS + TOPIC TESTS + SECTIONAL TESTS For RBI Gr. B, NABARD Gr. A, SEBI Gr. A, IFSCA Gr. A & SIDBI Gr. A Exams Web App BLOG FORUM Your one-stop destination for Interact with peers & experts, all examrelated information & exchange scores & improve preparation resources your preparation Explore Now Explore Now"], "a": null}]});
window.PYQ_OCR['nabard-a'].push({t:'nabard a 2021 decision making',q:[{"n": 91, "q": "Which is a structured method of group decision making which allows a rich generation of original ideas, behavioural participation of all members which reduces interaction of members at some point of the stage ?", "o": ["Delphi", "Brainstorming", "Nominal Group", "Fish bowling (e) Consensus mapping Answer – (c) Explanation - Nominal Group Technique gathers information by asking individuals to respond to questions posed by a moderator, and then asking participants to prioritize the ideas or suggestions of all group members."], "a": null}, {"n": 92, "q": "With a view to improve the process and outcomes of future decisions decision makers generally assess both outcome of a decision and process by which the decision has reached after –", "o": ["Analysing alternative course", "Decision has been made and implemented", "Evaluating alternative course of action", "Identifying alternative course of action (e) Defining and understanding the problem Answer – (c) Explanation - Rational decision-making processes consist of a sequence of steps designed to rationally develop a desired solution. The steps are as follows: 1. Identifying a problem or opportunity 2. Gathering information 3. Analysing the situation 4. Developing options 5. Evaluating options 6. Selecting a preferred alternative 7. Acting on the decision"], "a": null}, {"n": 93, "q": "Managers sometimes make decisions based on skills, knowledge & training. Such decisions are known as-", "o": ["Value ethics based decisions", "Experience based decisions", "Sub-conscious mental processing", "Cognitive based decisions (e) Environment based decisions Answer – (d) Explanation - This question can also be done using common sense and elimination method. Cognitive decision making aims specifically at information processing, conceptual resources, perceptual skill, language learning, and other aspects related to the development of the brain."], "a": null}, {"n": 94, "q": "Which of the following is an individual level factor that can affect process of decision making in an organisation?", "o": ["Personal values", "Economic Conditions", "Organisational politics", "Organisational policies (e) Government legislation Answer – (a) Explanation - All of the options except for option A are not factors at the individual level. Personal values greatly influence decision-making because they are deeply ingrained and impact our actions and behavior. Altruistic values have a positive effect on ethical decision-making, while self- enhancement values have a negative effect."], "a": null}, {"n": 95, "q": "Method of determining the root cause of the problem uses Boolean logic to determine cause of the problem in any undesirable event which involves a diagram that looks like a tree where all causes are written down as branches-", "o": ["Fault tree analysis", "Failure mode and effect analysis", "Eight D problem analysis", "Fishbone diagram (e) Five Whys analysis Answer – (a) Explanation - A fault tree is a diagram that displays the possible causes of a problem and how likely each cause is. The two main logic gates used in fault tree analysis are the AND Gate and the OR Gate."], "a": null}, {"n": 96, "q": "When a decision making wrongly comprises of two situations because of perceived similarity or evaluates an event without comparing it to the similar situations, the tendency is known as –", "o": ["Overconfidence bias", "Confirmation bias", "Time sight bias", "Availability bias (e) Representative bias Answer – (e) Explanation - The representativeness heuristic is when we judge how likely something is based on how much it resembles a familiar situation. It's a mental shortcut that helps us make quick and easy decisions."], "a": null}, {"n": 97, "q": "Which decision making theory was put forward, based on how the game of chess is played, and an individual’s relationship with uncertainty?", "o": ["Rational", "Prospect", "Bounded rationality", "Intuitive (e) Predispositioning Answer – (e) Explanation - Predispositioning theory was founded by Aron Katsenelinboigen, a professor in the Wharton School who dealt with indeterministic systems such as chess, business, economics, and other fields of knowledge and also made an essential step forward in elaboration of styles and methods of decision-making."], "a": null}, {"n": 98, "q": "Decision making technique useful in motivating participation in group decisions and which encourages all members to contribute at an individual level before being influenced by anyone else thereby leading to wide variety of ideas-", "o": ["Cost benefit analysis", "Step ladder technique", "Simulation training", "Star bursting (e) Heuristic method Answer – (b) Explanation - The stepladder technique is a structured procedure that facilitates effective group decision making. The goal is to ensure that the thoughts and ideas of all members are made available to the group so that they can be considered while the group is reaching a decision."], "a": null}, {"n": 99, "q": "Tendency to maintain things as they are even when that may be significantly less than the optimal is termed as -", "o": ["Sunk cost trap", "Prudence trap", "Anchoring trap", "Loss aversion trap (e) Status quo trap Answer – (e) Explanation - The status quo bias describes our preference for the current state of affairs; resulting in resistance to change."], "a": null}, {"n": 100, "q": "Leadership style where leader uses knowledge and past experience to reach a decision without seeking information from others-", "o": ["Directive Decision making style", "Delegating Decision making style", "Facilitative Decision-making style", "Conceptual Decision-making style (e) Analytical Decision-making style Answer – (a) Explanation - Since the question mentions ‘without seeking information from others’, so options B and C are out rightly eliminated. In analytical decision making style, decision maker examines much information before taking action and does not rely solely on knowledge and past experience. So, option E is also eliminated. Option D is also eliminated because leaders with this style evaluate different options and possibilities with a high tolerance to ambiguity. Free Ebooks Current Affairs Download Now Explore Now FREE MOCK TESTS + TOPIC TESTS + SECTIONAL TESTS For RBI Gr. B, NABARD Gr. A, SEBI Gr. A, IFSCA Gr. A & SIDBI Gr. A Exams Web App BLOG FORUM Your one-stop destination for Interact with peers & experts, all examrelated information & exchange scores & improve preparation resources your preparation Explore Now Explore Now"], "a": null}]});
window.PYQ_OCR['nabard-a'].push({t:'nabard a 2022 ard shift1',q:[{"n": 161, "q": "When major output is expected from per unit input focus is on factor of production (Land, Labour, Capital, Enterprise is called _____________.", "o": ["Agri diversification", "Agri intensification", "Agri exclusivity", "None of these (e) All of these Explanation - The key phrase “output is expected from per unit input” points to intensive agriculture. This suggests that agricultural intensification, which involves optimizing land, labor, capital, and enterprise, is the correct option."], "a": 1}, {"n": 162, "q": "MSP of Lentil of Rabi Marketing Season (2020-21) is __________.", "o": ["2015", "2050", "5500", "5400 (e) 4500"], "a": 2}, {"n": 163, "q": "Apna Khet Apna Kaam is the scheme of under MGNREGA in which of the following state?", "o": ["Rajasthan", "Punjab", "Haryana", "None of these (e) All of these"], "a": 0}, {"n": 164, "q": "Gestation period of Sheep is ____________.", "o": ["280 ± 3", "310±5", "150±5", "180±2 (e) None of these This question is from important chapter of “Animal Husbandry, Fisheries, Plantation and Horticulture”. So, every student should definitely expect such difficult questions."], "a": 2}, {"n": 165, "q": "Agriculture education day is celebrated on the birth anniversary of _______________.", "o": ["Rajendra Prasad", "C.C. Singh", "Venkatraman", "None of these (e) All of these"], "a": 0}, {"n": 166, "q": "A production system which avoids or largely excludes the use of synthetically compounded fertilizers, pesticides, growth regulators, genetically modified organisms and livestock food additives.", "o": ["Organic Farming", "Commercial Farming", "Extensive Farming", "None of these (e) All of these"], "a": 0}, {"n": 167, "q": "The popular breed of poultry which belongs to Italy.", "o": ["Plymouth rock", "Rhode Island Red", "White leghorn", "White leghorn Assel (e) New Hampshire"], "a": 2}, {"n": 168, "q": "The process by which fruits attain their desirable flavour, quality, colour, palatable nature and other textural properties.", "o": ["Degreening", "Ripening", "Curing", "Ethylene (e) Defreezing Explanation - Again, a conceptual question based on knowledge and various terms related to chapter of “Horticulture”."], "a": 1}, {"n": 169, "q": "Process of drop down of milk after the stimulation of oxytocin", "o": ["Mamogenesis", "Milk let down", "Squeezing", "Ejaculation (e) None of these Explanation - One more conceptual question from the Chapter of “Animal Husbandry”."], "a": 1}, {"n": 170, "q": "Development of interveinal chlorosis from bottom to top in later stages, purple colour and bronzing ultimately drying of plant parts", "o": ["Potassium", "Phosphorus", "Nitrogen", "None of these (e) All of these"], "a": 0}, {"n": 171, "q": "The modified stem that grow horizontally on the ground or below the ground are called___________.", "o": ["Runners", "Suckers", "Offsets", "Rhizomes (e) All of these"], "a": 0}, {"n": 172, "q": "__________ is a pan-India electronic trading portal which networks the existing APMC mandis to create a unified national market for agricultural commodities.", "o": ["e- NAM", "e- market", "E-kisan", "E- mandi (e) All of these"], "a": 0}, {"n": 173, "q": "According to the census of India 2011, What is the Percentage of Rural Population of India", "o": ["62.17%", "54.12%", "36.51%", "68.84% (e) None of these"], "a": 3}, {"n": 174, "q": "Contribution of agriculture and allied sector in Gross Value Added (GVA) for the 2021-22__________.", "o": ["7.9%", "15.5%", "17.2%", "12.7% (e) 18.8% Answer - (e)"], "a": null}, {"n": 175, "q": "In tractor economy, which of the following will be considered as fixed cost?", "o": ["Depreciation", "Maintenance", "Fuel and oil cost", "Repairs (e) None of the above"], "a": 0}, {"n": 176, "q": "Substances that contain microorganisms, which when added to the soil increase its fertility and promotes plant growth__________.", "o": ["Chemical fertilizers", "Biofertilizers", "Green manures", "Mulch crops (e) All of these"], "a": 1}, {"n": 177, "q": "What is the type of farming done along the contour of sloping land to avoid soil erosion with slope less than 33%.", "o": ["Graded bunding", "Bench terracing", "Contour farming", "Bunding (e) Stone terracing"], "a": 1}, {"n": 178, "q": "Aromatic plant botanical name- export and produce in India for perfume and fragrance", "o": ["jasmine", "portulaca", "champa", "marigold (e) None of these Explanation - Logic and observation also help in such questions cause jasmine and champa are having fragrance."], "a": 0}, {"n": 179, "q": "The water that held tightly on the surface of soil colloidal particle is known as …………….. It is essentially non-liquid and moves primarily in the vapour form", "o": ["Gravitational water", "Capillary water", "PWP", "Hygroscopic Water (e) Field capacity Explanation - Such concepts are very basic. Logically this concept is about “Characteristics of water”, which essentially is important topic from Soil and Irrigation/water resources Chapter."], "a": 3}, {"n": 180, "q": "A wax like substance containing the natural flower perfume together with some plant waxes, albumin and colouring matter.", "o": ["Yellow spot beetle", "Defoliator thrips", "Defoliator beetle", "None of these (e) All of these"], "a": 2}, {"n": 181, "q": "Damping Off of Papaya symptoms", "o": ["The disease prominently appears on green leaves and also on green immature fruits.", "The symptoms appear in the form of brown to black depressed spots on the fruits.", "The initial symptoms are water-soaked, sunken spots on the fruit.", "The centres of these spots later turn black and then pink when the fungus produces spores (e) None of these"], "a": 0}, {"n": 182, "q": "Coconut is propagated through?", "o": ["Budding", "Grafting", "Layering", "Seedlings (e) None of the above"], "a": 3}, {"n": 183, "q": "Climate smart agriculture does not include ______.", "o": ["Increased productivity, Enhanced resilience & Reduced emissions", "Bridge a knowledge gap by providing clarity on CSA terminology, components, relevant issues, and how to contextualize them under different country conditions.", "Better nutrition, a better environment and a better life for all, leaving no one behind", "Increase in the production with ecology Sustainability (e) Ecosystem Balance"], "a": 0}, {"n": 184, "q": "Farming so as to meet society's present food and textile needs, without compromising the ability for current or future generations to meet their needs.", "o": ["Sustainable agriculture", "Shifting Agriculture", "Natural farming", "Permaculture (e) None of the above"], "a": 0}, {"n": 185, "q": "The deficiency in plants can be visually identified at the early vegetative stage as an abnormally dark green or reddish, purple colour along the edge of the lower plant leaves", "o": ["Potassium", "Phosphorus", "Nitrogen", "Calcium (e) Boron"], "a": 1}, {"n": 186, "q": "Botanical Name of Teak is called?", "o": ["Grevellia robusta", "Casuarina equisetifolia", "Ailanthus ultisima", "Terminalia arjuna (e) Tectonia Grandis Answer - (e)"], "a": null}, {"n": 187, "q": "Whitish-gray powdery coating on the leaves or fruit. On leaves, initial symptoms appear as chlorotic spots on the upper leaf surface that soon become whitish lesions is the symptom seen in grapes, roses and other aromatic crops are due to which disease?", "o": ["Downey Mildew", "Powdery mildew", "Anthracnose", "Collar Rot (e) None of the above"], "a": 0}, {"n": 188, "q": "Highest cut rose sold in which day of the year", "o": ["Rose Day", "Valentine’s Day", "Mothers day", "Fathers Day (e) Xmas Day"], "a": 1}, {"n": 189, "q": "Which organelle responsible for growth and development", "o": ["Cytoplasm", "Nucleus", "Ribosome", "Mitochondria (e) None of the above"], "a": 1}, {"n": 190, "q": "Ram lamb is castrated at what age", "o": ["07-10 Days", "1-2 Weeks", "2-4 Weeks 4.", "4-10 Weeks (e) > 14 Weeks"], "a": 2}, {"n": 191, "q": "What should be the pH for the Fish-pond for fish culture?", "o": ["6.5-10", "4-4.5", "11-14", "4.5-5 (e) None of the above"], "a": 0}, {"n": 192, "q": "Agroforestry system in which long fodder crops are grown to protect the soil, mulching and to prevent erosion.", "o": ["Silvi pastoral", "Taungya", "woody hedges", "Shifting agriculture (e) Acqua- Forestry"], "a": 0}, {"n": 193, "q": "Grape’s leaf feeding in initial stage and complete defoliation is caused by", "o": ["Defoliator beetle", "Defoliator thrips", "Defoliator Aphids", "Defoliator jassids (e) None of these"], "a": 0}, {"n": 194, "q": "__________involves the participation and collaboration of various stakeholders including community, government and nongovernmental organisations fir the timber, wood collection", "o": ["Social Forestry", "Community forestry", "Extension Forestry", "Farm Forestry (e) None of the above"], "a": 1}, {"n": 195, "q": "What is the GVA share of agriculture sector according to the First Income estimates", "o": ["18.4", "20.2", "18.8", "19.6 (e) 15.4"], "a": 0}, {"n": 196, "q": "Any surface area from which runoff resulting from rainfall is collected and drained through a common point.", "o": ["Watershed management", "Rain water Harvesting", "Hygroscopic coefficient", "None of these (e) All of these"], "a": 0}, {"n": 197, "q": "Scheme which is used to assess the current status of soil health and, when used over time, to determine changes in soil health that are affected by land management.", "o": ["Pradhan mantri Kisan Maan Dhan Yojana", "Soil Health Card", "eNAM", "PKVY (e) None of the above"], "a": 1}, {"n": 198, "q": "An integral part of the National Agricultural Research System (NARS), aims at assessment of location specific technology modules in agriculture", "o": ["ATMA", "KVK", "Esharam", "E shakti (e) None"], "a": 1}, {"n": 199, "q": "Scheme for the solution of all the problems of farmers", "o": ["Kisan Call Centres", "E Krishi Samvad", "E kishi Mela", "None of these (e) All of these"], "a": 0}, {"n": 200, "q": "Which one of the following is Indian Major Carps", "o": ["Catla", "Labeo Rohita", "Cyprinus Carpio", "None of these (e) All of these Explanation - This question requires observation+ knowledge. If you are not versed with the Major carps at all, you might find this question difficult. A through reading of chapters like Fisheries, Animal Husbandry is required. Free Ebooks Current Affairs Download Now Explore Now FREE MOCK TESTS + TOPIC TESTS + SECTIONAL TESTS For RBI Gr. B, NABARD Gr. A, SEBI Gr. A, IFSCA Gr. A & SIDBI Gr. A Exams Web App BLOG FORUM Your one-stop destination for Interact with peers & experts, all examrelated information & exchange scores & improve preparation resources your preparation Explore Now Explore Now"], "a": 0}]});
window.PYQ_OCR['nabard-a'].push({t:'nabard a 2022 decision making shift1',q:[{"n": 91, "q": "Which of the following is a quantitative method of decision making?", "o": ["PERT", "Rule of thumb", "Psychological analysis", "Decision making by creativity (e) Following standard procedure Answer – (a) Explanation - PERT stands for Performance Evaluation and Review Technique. All the techniques except PERT are qualitative methods."], "a": null}, {"n": 92, "q": "Tendency to see a particular situation or issue from chosen perspective, influencing our ability to understand alternative or conflicting points of view or alternatives is called", "o": ["Availability bias", "Immediate gratification", "Status quo bias", "Hindsight bias (e) Selective perception Answer – (e) Explanation - Selective perception occurs when the perceiver singles out certain information that supports or reinforces a prior belief and filters out information that does not confirm that belief. Selective perception relates closely to confirmation bias."], "a": null}, {"n": 93, "q": "Which of the following problem-solving tools is a visual means of displaying the sequence of activities and decisions that occur in a system or process over time?", "o": ["Brainstorming", "Benchmarking", "Flowchart", "Five Whys Analysis (e) Force Field Analysis Answer – (c) Explanation - A flowchart is a diagram that shows the sequence of actions or events in a process or a system. It uses different shapes and symbols to represent the elements and the relationships between them. For example, a rectangle represents a task or an operation, a diamond represents a decision or a condition, and an arrow represents the direction of the flow. Flowcharts help to break down a complex problem into smaller and simpler steps and organize them in a logical order."], "a": null}, {"n": 94, "q": "One of the barriers to good decision making is setting out to solve wrong problem because we have created a mental framework for our decision, with little thought, that causes us to overlook the best option or lose sight of important objectives. This is called", "o": ["Failure to interpret feedback", "Frame blindness", "Not keeping track", "Over confidence in our judgement (e) Short sighted shortcuts Answer – (b) Explanation - Russo and Schoemaker have identified ten most common barriers that we often encounter in making good decisions in their book titled ‘Decision Traps’. One of the taps in ‘frame blindness’ which could be avoided by understanding frames."], "a": null}, {"n": 95, "q": "The type of Data Analytics which is used to make forecasts about future trends and answer the question ‘What might happen in the future’ is called", "o": ["Inferential analytics", "Descriptive analytics", "Predictive analytics", "Diagnostic analytics (e) Prescriptive analytics Answer – (c) Explanation - This is a factual question but can be answered if you know the meaning of ‘Predictive’. Predictive analytics is the use of data to predict future trends and events. It uses historical data to forecast potential scenarios that can help drive strategic decisions."], "a": null}, {"n": 96, "q": "Most ‘judgemental problems’ are solved by", "o": ["use of good judgement & minimizing possibility of undesired outcomes", "habitual response, standard operating procedure", "inventory reorder model, queueing theory, statistical analysis", "frequent modification in strategies to match development in technology (e) computational techniques like linear programming and network analysis Answer – (a) Explanation - This is a very generic question which can be answered by eliminating the options or choosing the most accurate answer. In decision making, some generic questions are also being asked which can be answered using common sense."], "a": null}, {"n": 97, "q": "In Root Cause Analysis (RCA), which of the following is the cause in case people did something wrong or did not do something that was needed?", "o": ["physical cause", "organizational cause", "statutory cause", "legislative cause (e) human cause Answer – (e) Explanation - Root Cause Analysis (RCA) is a popular and often-used technique that helps people answer the question of why the problem occurred in the first place. There are three basic type of causes under RCA: Physical causes, Human causes and Organizational causes."], "a": null}, {"n": 98, "q": "Effective communication during decision making process will help to minimize", "o": ["resistance and negative emotions", "interest and receptivity", "necessary support for changes", "harmony and agreement (e) support and cooperation Answer – (a) Explanation - All the other options except option A are positive attributes. So, the question speaks about minimization and we will naturally want to eliminate something which is negative. Hence, Option A is the right answer."], "a": null}, {"n": 99, "q": "Overconfidence about our judgement abilities and prediction accuracy, as we remember our successes and quickly forget our errors is called", "o": ["Overconfidence trap", "Estimating trap", "Anchoring trap", "Information overdose trap (e) Confirming evidence trap Answer – (a) Explanation - Daniel Kahnemann and Amos Tversky found that individuals are influenced by overconfidence bias, hindsight bias, anchoring bias, framing bias, and escalation of commitment. Overconfidence bias occurs when individuals overestimate their ability to predict future events."], "a": null}, {"n": 100, "q": "Which of the following decision making style is suitable for a leader where there are more than one right answer and where cause effect relationship is discoverable but not immediately apparent?", "o": ["avoidant style", "conceptual style", "behavioural style", "analytic style (e) directive style Answer – (d) Explanation - Analytic decision-makers examine much information before taking action. For example, analytic leaders rely on direct observation, data, and facts to support their decisions. These decision-makers have a high tolerance for ambiguity and are very adaptable, but they like to control most aspects of the decision process. This style is a well-rounded approach to decision-making but can be time-consuming. Free Ebooks Current Affairs Download Now Explore Now FREE MOCK TESTS + TOPIC TESTS + SECTIONAL TESTS For RBI Gr. B, NABARD Gr. A, SEBI Gr. A, IFSCA Gr. A & SIDBI Gr. A Exams Web App BLOG FORUM Your one-stop destination for Interact with peers & experts, all examrelated information & exchange scores & improve preparation resources your preparation Explore Now Explore Now"], "a": null}]});

